using System;using System.IO;
// Per-job skill rules, generated from skill/<job>skill.lst and each .skl by
// local-run/pvf/gen_skill_rules.py (mapping: local-run/recon/role-create-jobs-report.md s7).
// Skill ids are per job (reference find_skill(job, index)), so the single swordman table in
// Skill-Rules-FG38.cs cannot answer for the other eight creatable jobs.
// SkillClass/Fitness/Trait feed Offline70SkillSlots.TabBaseFG273, the reform_ui_group_no
// tab rule; every other field is the SP learn rule. GrowCaps is the pre-awakening ceiling
// ([growtype maximum level] x [skill fitness growtype]) and AwakenCaps the post-awakening
// one ([second growtype maximum level] column 2*grow); Offline70SkillSlots.JobMaximum picks
// the GrowCaps entry while the character has no first awakening, so a level-60/70 skill
// stays unbuyable until the awakening byte is set, which is what the native client gates on.
